  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Support the presser – five v four",
  "description": "A pitch of about 40 × 50 metres with a full-size goal and goalkeeper at one end and two small goals at the other. Four blue attackers plus a free player, J, against five red defenders. J always starts with the ball and only plays as support from behind.\n\nRed have an extra player and must use it: one presses, one supports close by and the rest cover the space in front of goal. The attempt ends when red win the ball, after a goal or when the ball goes out. Swap attack and defence after ten attempts and change the free player at the same time.\n\nBuild on it: let red score in the small goals after winning the ball. Harder: five v five, with J free to play anywhere. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The supporting defender stands two or three metres at an angle behind the presser – close enough to take over at once."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "When the ball moves on, the supporter becomes the new presser and the old presser drops back to become the new support."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The rest move with the ball and stay compact – no free space straight in front of goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The goalkeeper sees the whole picture: organise the defence with your voice."
    }
  ],
